kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  add_requirement,tui50,"streaming-mutable-last-line","The TUI streaming render MUST grow the in-progress (not-yet-newline-terminated) text in the mutable last line at the top of the tail region (visually continuous with the scrollback above), rendered within the ratatui buffer (inline viewport), NOT via direct terminal escape-sequence writes that bypass the ratatui buffer. Complete newline-terminated lines MUST be committed incrementally to the scrollback via insert_before as soon as their newline boundary arrives (not batched until turn end). The tail region MUST contain only: the mutable last line (top, redrawn each frame in the buffer, transparent background so it blends into the scrollback), the thinking/status indicator, and the input prompt (bottom). The mutable last line MUST wrap to multiple rows when it exceeds the terminal width (honoring CJK display width); rows beyond the tail capacity are dropped from the top (content is not lost — it commits to scrollback on the next newline). TurnEnd MUST flush any residual un-terminated text to the scrollback. The newline-gated buffer (drain_complete_lines on newline, pending_tail for the un-terminated remainder) is the core mechanism, modeled on codex MarkdownStreamCollector in simplified form (no markdown parsing, no table holdback, no animation chunking). Evidence: the escape-sequence implementation (raw_render.rs) had committed and mutable lines both write physical row viewport_top-1, overwriting each other, and TurnEnd clear_mutable erased committed content (the reply-cleared-after-stream bug); codex StreamController grows the active cell in place each frame within the buffer.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui51,"render-layer-componentized","The TUI rendering layer MUST be decomposed into reusable, self-contained widgets under the tui components directory, each consuming only UI-only data types (RenderedLine, a string, spinner index, input buffer), each independently verifiable via a TestBackend, and each composable by a layout widget (Tail) that bottom-anchors its children. At minimum: TranscriptLine (RenderedLine into Buffer for the insert_before commit path), MutableLine (pending tail at tail buffer top, wrapped, transparent bg), ThinkingIndicator (spinner plus label), InputPrompt (prompt plus input plus cursor plus input_bg block, CJK-aware cursor), Tail (composes the above, bottom-anchored, capacity-aware top-drop). draw_tail_frame MUST delegate to Tail render; commit_to_scrollback MUST consume a slice of RenderedLine and render via TranscriptLine. The rendering layer MUST NOT use direct terminal escape-sequence writes (raw escape or DECSTBM scroll-region manipulation) that bypass the ratatui buffer — such code is not widget-able (bound to physical coordinates), not TestBackend-verifiable (violates tui41), and bypasses the RenderedLine seam (violates tui42). Evidence: user goal that every TUI part be an explainable, reusable, individually-verifiable widget (component); the escape route (raw_render.rs) was the one non-widget-able part and produced the reply-cleared bug.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[4]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui50,"complete-lines-commit-incrementally","a TextDelta containing a newline arrives during a turn","the event is handled","the complete line before the newline is committed to scrollback immediately via insert_before (not held until TurnEnd)"
  tui50,"pending-tail-grows-in-tail-top","streaming text without a newline is arriving","the tail frame is rendered each frame","the un-terminated text appears in the top row of the tail region (mutable last line) growing in place within the ratatui buffer and the thinking indicator sits below it and the input prompt at the bottom"
  tui51,"widgets-independently-testable","each widget under the tui components directory is exercised","it is rendered to a TestBackend buffer and asserted","TranscriptLine, MutableLine, ThinkingIndicator, InputPrompt, Tail each render their expected content independently without a real terminal"
  tui51,"no-escape-direct-write","the tui source is inspected for escape-sequence rendering","raw_render.rs and any DECSTBM or MoveTo-then-Print bypass of the ratatui buffer are checked","no escape-sequence direct-write rendering path exists; all rendering goes through the ratatui buffer"
